---
import LegalPage from "../components/shared/legal-page/index.astro";

const title = "Andesine Privacy Policy";
const description = "How Vrite, Inc. collects, uses, and protects data in Andesine.";
---

<LegalPage title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/">
  <h1>Andesine Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Effective date: November 9, 2026. Last updated: November 9, 2026.</p>
  <p>
    This policy explains what data Andesine collects, why we collect it, who we share it with, how
    long we keep it, and what choices you have.
  </p>

  <h3>1. Who we are</h3>
  <p>
    Andesine is operated by Vrite, Inc., a Delaware corporation ("we", "us"). Our address is 1111B S
    Governors Ave STE 6387, Dover, DE 19904, United States. For privacy questions and requests,
    email
    <a href="mailto:support@andesine.app">support@andesine.app</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For account data, analytics, and billing, we are the data controller. For the content in your
    workspace, we process it to provide the service on behalf of the workspace and its admins.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Scope</h3>
  <p>
    This policy applies to Andesine Cloud: the website and app at
    <a href="https://andesine.app">andesine.app</a>, the API at <code>api.andesine.app</code>
    (including the MCP server), sites that you publish on <code>andesine.page</code>, and our
    extensions, such as GitHub Sync.
  </p>
  <p>
    It does not apply to self-hosted Andesine. The operator of a self-hosted instance is responsible
    for the data on it. Self-hosted instances do not send analytics to us.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Data we collect</h3>
  <h4>Account data</h4>
  <p>
    Your name, email address, and profile image. If you sign in with Google or GitHub, we receive
    your name, email address, and profile image from that provider, and we keep the tokens that the
    provider gives us.
  </p>
  <h4>Sign-in and security data</h4>
  <p>
    Sessions, with the IP address and browser user agent of each session. Passkeys (the public key
    and device type only). One-time sign-in codes, which we store hashed.
  </p>
  <h4>Workspace content</h4>
  <p>
    The entries, collections, schemas, versions, images, and files that you and your team add. To
    make content searchable, we create search embeddings of it. For images, we create a text
    description and extract visible text.
  </p>
  <h4>Collaboration data</h4>
  <p>
    Workspace memberships and roles, the email addresses of people you invite, and which members
    contributed to each version.
  </p>
  <h4>Billing data</h4>
  <p>
    Stripe processes payments. Stripe keeps your card details and tax ID; we do not receive your
    full card number. We keep your Stripe customer ID, plan, subscription status, spending limit,
    usage counts, and the billing events that Stripe sends us.
  </p>
  <h4>Connected apps, API keys, and integrations</h4>
  <p>
    The apps that you connect (for example, AI assistants through MCP), their access tokens, and the
    access that you granted. API keys (we store a hash and an encrypted copy). Webhook URLs,
    secrets, and delivery history. Extension settings and data. For GitHub Sync, the contents of the
    repositories that you connect.
  </p>
  <h4>Usage and analytics data</h4>
  <p>
    Events about how you use Andesine, such as sign-ins, created workspaces, published entries, and
    searches. These events contain IDs, not your content. See section 6.
  </p>
  <h4>Technical logs</h4>
  <p>
    Our hosting providers log requests, including the IP address, time, and path, to run and protect
    the service.
  </p>
  <h4>Support messages</h4>
  <p>The messages that you send us, and the data in them.</p>

  <h3>4. How we use data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To provide Andesine</strong>: accounts, workspaces, editing, collaboration, search,
      publishing, the API, connected apps, and extensions. Legal basis: contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To keep the service secure</strong>: sign-in, abuse prevention, rate limits, and
      investigations. Legal basis: legitimate interests.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To bill you</strong>: subscriptions, usage, invoices, and taxes. Legal basis: contract
      and legal obligation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To send emails</strong>: sign-in codes, session checks, invitations, spending alerts,
      and significant updates. We do not send regular marketing emails. Legal basis: contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To improve Andesine</strong>: usage data that contain IDs only. Legal basis:
      legitimate interests.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To comply with the law</strong> and to protect our rights. Legal basis: legal obligation
      and legitimate interests.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data. We do not use it for targeted advertising.</p>

  <h3>5. AI features</h3>
  <p>
    Search, Ask AI, and image analysis use OpenAI. When these features run, we send OpenAI the
    content that they need: entry text for search embeddings, images for descriptions and text
    extraction, and, for Ask AI, your question, recent messages in the conversation, and the
    matching parts of your content.
  </p>
  <p>
    OpenAI does not use data sent through its API to train its models. OpenAI can keep this data for
    up to 30 days to detect abuse, and then deletes it.
  </p>

  <h3>6. Cookies and local storage</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Necessary</strong>: the session cookies that keep you signed in (up to 7 days), and
      layout preferences such as panel sizes. These do not need consent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent</strong>: the <code>andesine-consent</code> cookie saves your choice for 1 year.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics</strong>: PostHog cookies - on website, only if you accept, and in product.
      If you decline, we count visits without cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local storage</strong>: the app keeps a copy of workspace content in your browser to
      work offline and load faster. Signing out clears it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>7. Who we share data with</h3>
  <p>We share data with these service providers, only to run Andesine:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Render</strong> (United States): hosting, database, search, and background jobs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (global): network, website and app delivery, file storage, and hosting
      of published sites and extensions.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> (United States): payments, invoices, and taxes.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> (United States): email delivery.</li>
    <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> (United States): AI features (section 5).</li>
    <li><strong>PostHog</strong> (United States): product analytics.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google and GitHub</strong>: sign-in, if you choose it. <strong>GitHub</strong>: GitHub
      Sync, if you connect a repository.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We also share data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>With your workspace</strong>: members see your name, email address, profile image, and
      your contributions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>With the public, when you publish</strong>: published content can be read by anyone
      who has the workspace's publishable key, and sites on <code>andesine.page</code> are public.
    </li>
    <li><strong>With apps that you connect</strong> (section 8).</li>
    <li>
      <strong>When the law requires it</strong>, or to protect the rights and safety of others.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>In a business transfer</strong>, such as a merger or acquisition, under this policy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>8. Connected apps</h3>
  <p>
    When you connect an app, such as an AI assistant through MCP, you choose one workspace and read
    or write access. The app can do only what your role in that workspace allows. Access tokens
    expire after 15 minutes, and the app renews them for up to 30 days without use.
  </p>
  <p>
    To remove an app's access, go to <strong>Settings → Personal → Connected apps</strong> and revoke
    it. This deletes its tokens at once. Data that the app already received is under that app's privacy
    policy.
  </p>

  <h3>9. How long we keep data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data</strong>: until you delete your account. Then we delete your account,
      sessions, sign-in methods, connected apps, and profile image, and your analytics data in
      PostHog.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Workspaces</strong>: until an admin deletes the workspace. Deletion is immediate and
      removes its content, versions, files, and search index. If you delete your account and you are
      the only admin of a workspace, that workspace is deleted too. In other workspaces, your
      content stays, without your name on it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Automatic versions and webhook history</strong>: 7 days on the Free plan, 30 days on
      the Pro plan. Named and published versions stay until you delete them.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Unused files</strong>: 7 days after no entry uses them.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing records</strong>: as long as tax and accounting laws require, also after you
      delete a workspace or account.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Backups</strong>: up to 7 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs</strong>: up to 30 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Support messages</strong>: as long as we need them to help you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>10. International transfers</h3>
  <p>
    We store and process data in the United States. When we transfer personal data from the European
    Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, we rely on the Standard Contractual Clauses
    and other safeguards that our service providers offer.
  </p>

  <h3>11. Security</h3>
  <p>
    We encrypt data in transit. We store API keys, sign-in codes, and webhook secrets hashed or
    encrypted. Access to production systems is limited. No system is fully secure, so we cannot
    guarantee security. If a breach affects your data, we will tell you as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h3>12. Your rights</h3>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give you access to, or a copy of, your personal data;</li>
    <li>correct it;</li>
    <li>delete it;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we use it;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent, at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can edit your profile and delete your account in the app settings. For other requests, email <a
      href="mailto:support@andesine.app">support@andesine.app</a
    > from the email address of your account. We reply within 30 days. We do not treat you differently
    for using your rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in the EEA, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, you can also complain to your data
    protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>California residents</strong>: we collect the categories of data in section 3 for the
    purposes in section 4, from you, your workspace, and the providers you sign in with. We do not
    sell or share personal data for cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not respond to Do
    Not Track signals.
  </p>

  <h3>13. Children</h3>
  <p>
    Andesine is not for people under 16. We do not knowingly collect data from them. If you think a
    child gave us data, email us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h3>14. Changes</h3>
  <p>
    We will post changes on this page and update the date above. If a change is significant, we will
    tell you by email or in the app before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h3>15. Contact</h3>
  <p>
    Vrite, Inc.
    <br />
    1111B S Governors Ave STE 6387
    <br />
    Dover, DE 19904, United States
    <br />
    <a href="mailto:support@andesine.app">support@andesine.app</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
